use /lib
from /scope/project-locations import ProjectLocationsScope
from /scope/prompt-mode/modes import PromptModesScope

export shape TaskTableOutcomeShape:
    description:
        Once a run is over, its final summary is headed by a row of small
        tags saying what the run did, so what came of any prompt, a task or a
        question, can be told at a glance. The final summary is the reply
        text the run gave after its last tool call, or the final result shown
        in its place; the tags head the last row of that text. They sit above
        the row's text, in its Output cell, with a little room beneath them,
        left to right in the order below, wrapping onto another line if the
        cell is too narrow. Each is a small label in extra small text, with a
        little padding either side and slightly rounded corners, 4 pixels
        from the next. A run that gave no reply text after its last tool
        call, such as one that failed or was cancelled before it gave one,
        shows its tags on its last row instead, whatever that row is.

    tags:
        Each tag is shown only when it applies, worked out from what the run
        did, not from what it was asked or what it said:

        - "Wrote spec", in Spec's colour, when it wrote or edited a file in the spec location, as the @{ProjectLocationsScope} says, or under .claude/reference
        - "Wrote code", in Code's colour, when it wrote or edited a file in the code location, the project config's codeRoot
        - "Wrote files", in the theme's muted grey, when it wrote or edited a file in neither, outside the project's own data in .suspense
        - "Answered", in Ask's colour, when it wrote or edited no file at all, or only files in .suspense, and gave a final summary, as a question almost always does
        - "No changes", in the theme's muted grey, when it wrote or edited no such file and gave no final summary

        So a run shows one or more of the first three, or exactly one of the
        last two. The spec location is the one the task was sent against, as
        its compiled prompt records, or for a run that doesn't record one,
        the project config's root; a project whose config gives no codeRoot
        has no code location, and nothing counts as code in it.

        A file counts as written or edited when the run's tool calls report
        writing or editing it, with a file tool or a shell command, as the
        referenced spec works them out, a subagent's included; a file only
        read never counts. Each colour is its mode's, as the
        @{PromptModesScope} colours it, including any colour chosen in the
        theme editor. The label is in the colour at full strength, on a faint
        tint of it, about a sixth of its strength, readable in light and dark
        mode.

    notWhileRunning:
        While the run is under way, no tags are shown; they appear once it is
        over, however it ended, done, failed, or cancelled. A task or question restored from the
        history, among the previous tasks or answers, shows them as its record
        replays, worked out against the project it belongs to, the same as
        when it ran.
